===Etymology 2===
From English dialectal {{m|en|eid}}, from {{der|en|non|eið|t=an isthmus, neck of land}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*aidiją|t=isthmus, strait}}, of uncertain origin, but probably from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁ey-|t=to go}}. Cognate with {{cog|is|eið}}, {{m|is|eiði}}, {{cog|fo|eið}}, {{m|fo|eiði|t=isthmus}}, {{cog|no|eid|t=isthmus}}, {{cog|sv|ed}}. Compare {{cog|la|eō|t=go, proceed|pos=verb}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ed}}, {{l|en|aith}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialectal|Scotland}} An [[isthmus]] or narrow neck of land jutting out into the sea; a [[sandbank]] cast up by the sea across the head of an open [[bight]] or inlet and having a lagoon inside it.

